message:
Fix GetRealHeroForMultiOutputFusion method for regular fusions.

In case the fusion is not a multi-output fusion (yet),
GetRealHeroForMultiOutputFusion should still try to find a "Reduce hero" or a
"Transpose hero" (if they exist).
Otherwise the check in ShapesCompatibleForMultiOutputFusion will compare the
wrong shapes.

Without this fix, we would run into a CHECK failure in ir_emitter_unnested for this
HLO module, because it would (wrongly) create a multi-output fusion:

HloModule fusion

ENTRY main {
  param_0.164 = f32[1024,1024,1024]{2,1,0} parameter(0)
  slice = f32[1024,256,512]{2,1,0} slice(param_0.164), slice={[0:1024:1], [0:256:1], [0:512:1]}
  slice2 = f32[256,512,1024]{2,1,0} slice(param_0.164), slice={[0:256:1], [0:512:1], [0:1024:1]}
  transpose.234 = f32[1024,512,256]{2,1,0} transpose(slice), dimensions={0,2,1}
  bitcast.1502 = f32[134217728]{0} reshape(transpose.234)
  transpose.232.clone.1 = f32[1024,512,256]{2,1,0} transpose(slice2), dimensions={2,1,0}
  bitcast.1494.clone.1 = f32[134217728]{0} reshape(transpose.232.clone.1)
  ROOT tuple.3 = (f32[134217728]{0}, f32[134217728]{0}) tuple(bitcast.1502, bitcast.1494.clone.1)
}

